---
alwaysApply: false
---

- New specs are written in ./docs/spec/**/<spec_name>.md.
- Specs location also define the location of the code to be implemented.
- Specs must specify where the code should be implemented.
- The spec document may reference other spec documents, but should not depend on them. Use @ref to reference other spec documents. Use @todo to mark sections that are not yet implemented.
- Specs should be concise and to the point, avoid unnecessary detail but make sure to cover all the details.
- Spec should include section for exception, see ./docs/spec/exceptions.md for the exception system design. You should always use subclasses of PrgitError, favor creating new subclasses for common issues.
- Spec should show the interface of the code to be implemented, including types and parameters.
- Spec should not contain a testing strategy section.
- Spec should contain a usage example section.